message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "AgriDesign: a browser-based platform for the design and analysis of agricultural experiments"
abstract: >-
  AgriDesign is a self-contained web application for planning and analysing agricultural
  experiments entirely in the browser, with no installation and no server-side computation.
  It covers data import with tidy-format checks, descriptive statistics, verification of the
  ANOVA assumptions with transformations and non-parametric alternatives, the classical
  experimental designs (CRD, RCBD, Latin square, incomplete blocks, augmented, factorials,
  split-plot, strip-plot, split-split-plot, nested, ANCOVA) with their error strata and eleven
  mean-separation procedures, editable publication-quality figures, an automatic report, and a
  generator of randomised field layouts, field books and replicate/power calculations.
